# Remote build execution (RBE) — generated by `bazel run //tools/remote:setup`.
# Non-secret + committed. The API key lives in the git-ignored user.bazelrc.
# Opt in per build with `--config=remote` (never breaks offline/local builds).
common:remote --remote_executor=grpcs://remote.buildbuddy.io
common:remote --remote_cache=grpcs://remote.buildbuddy.io
common:remote --bes_backend=grpcs://remote.buildbuddy.io
common:remote --bes_results_url=https://app.buildbuddy.io/invocation/
common:remote --remote_timeout=10m
common:remote --jobs=50
common:remote --remote_download_outputs=minimal
# Default Linux execution platform/container for RBE actions. The image must ship
# a modern glibc (>=2.28) for current Node/Python toolchains AND a modern git
# (>=2.28) for tests/tools that use `git init -b`, `git switch`, etc. Ubuntu
# 22.04 (rbe-ubuntu22-04) provides git 2.34 / glibc 2.35; the older 20.04 image
# ships git 2.25 (no `git init -b`). Adjust to match your toolchains. NOTE: macOS
# targets cannot run on Linux RBE — keep them local (e.g. --strategy=...=local).
# See docs/remote-build.md.
common:remote --remote_default_exec_properties=OSFamily=linux
common:remote --remote_default_exec_properties=container-image=docker://gcr.io/flame-public/rbe-ubuntu22-04:latest

# Cache-only profile (--config=remotecache): share the BuildBuddy remote cache +
# BES but WITHOUT remote execution. Unlike :remote it sets NO --remote_executor
# and NO --remote_download_outputs=minimal, so build OUTPUTS stay materialized
# locally and actions run on the runner. Use this on lanes that consume
# bazel-bin artifacts directly (image push, `cp` of a built zip, a vendored
# schema-engine binary) or need host-local test execution (Playwright/Chromium),
# where full RBE would break them. Remote-cache I/O errors fall back to local
# execution; BES upload is fully async so it never blocks or fails the build.
# CI variant of :remotecache. Identical, PLUS uploading the results of locally
# executed actions so the shared cache actually gets populated.
#
# WHY IT IS SEPARATE FROM :remotecache. tools/preset.bazelrc:138 sets
# `common --noremote_upload_local_results` always-on, deliberately: it stops a
# DEVELOPER's local build from poisoning the shared cache. preset.bazelrc:142
# flips it back under `--config=ci` -- but nothing ever passes `--config=ci`
# (#1267), so the flip never happened on CI either. Net effect: the six
# :remotecache lanes execute LOCALLY (cache-only, no remote executor) and were
# only ever able to READ a cache that nothing populated. :remotecache stays
# upload-free so it remains safe as a local-developer default (#506).
#
# WHY NOT JUST ADD `--config=ci` TO THOSE LANES. Measured 2026-07-27: :ci also
# carries `--remote_download_outputs=minimal` (preset.bazelrc:122), and on a
# CACHE HIT that does not materialise top-level outputs. Same target, same disk
# cache: a normal build produced tabula-extension-chrome.zip (322k); the same
# build with `minimal` reported "Build completed successfully" with 497 cache
# hits and NO zip on disk. The artifact lanes (`chrome_zip` -> `gh release
# upload`, the image push, the migrate binary) would have published nothing off
# a green build. So this profile takes the upload flag and NOT the download
# semantics. Adopting the rest of :ci needs `--remote_download_outputs=toplevel`
# alongside it on any lane that consumes a built artifact.
common:remotecache-ci --config=remotecache
common:remotecache-ci --remote_upload_local_results

common:remotecache --remote_cache=grpcs://remote.buildbuddy.io
common:remotecache --bes_backend=grpcs://remote.buildbuddy.io
common:remotecache --bes_results_url=https://app.buildbuddy.io/invocation/
common:remotecache --bes_upload_mode=fully_async
common:remotecache --remote_timeout=10m
